.TH FAIL2ZIG.TOML 5 "2026-09-10" "fail2zig 0.3.1" "File Formats"
.
.SH NAME
fail2zig.toml \- fail2zig daemon configuration file
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/fail2zig/config.toml
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fail2zig.toml
is the configuration file for the
.BR fail2zig (1)
intrusion prevention daemon. The file uses a strict subset of the TOML format.
.PP
Unknown keys are rejected with line and column context. Unknown sections are
rejected. All values are strictly typed; a string where an integer is expected
is an error.
.PP
The file is divided into three section types:
.IP \(bu 2
.B [global]
\(em daemon-wide settings (log level, socket path, memory ceiling, metrics listener, firewall backend).
.IP \(bu 2
.B [defaults]
\(em default values applied to every jail unless overridden.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR [jails. \fIname\fR ]
\(em one section per jail, overriding any defaults as needed.
.PP
Validate the configuration without starting the daemon:
.PP
.nf
sudo fail2zig --validate-config --config /etc/fail2zig/config.toml
.fi
.
.SH GLOBAL SECTION
.TP
.B log_level
String. One of
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.BR warn ,
.BR err .
Default:
.IR info .
.TP
.B pid_file
String (absolute path). Deprecated compatibility key; an explicit setting logs
a warning and no PID file is created. Use systemd MainPID. Default:
.IR /run/fail2zig/fail2zig.pid .
.TP
.B socket_path
String (absolute path). Unix domain socket for
.BR fail2zig\-client (1).
Default:
.IR /run/fail2zig/fail2zig.sock .
Mode 0660; group
.B fail2zig
if that group exists.
.TP
.B websocket_max_clients
Integer (1–1024). Maximum simultaneous WebSocket clients. Default: 16.
.TP
.B state_file
String (absolute path). Ban-state file, written on clean shutdown and read at
startup. CRC32-validated; discarded on mismatch. Mode 0600. Default:
.IR /var/lib/fail2zig/state.bin .
.TP
.B memory_ceiling_mb
Integer. Bounds the state tracker's entry capacity: the ceiling is divided by
an approximate per-entry size (~1536\ B) to derive a maximum tracked-IP count.
Once that cap is reached, the oldest unbanned entries are evicted rather than
growing unbounded. This is not a per-component byte budget on every allocator.
Minimum: 16. Default: 64.
.TP
.B metrics_enabled
Boolean. When
.IR false ,
no HTTP or WebSocket listener is bound; the daemon logs
.I "http: disabled by config"
and the startup banner shows
.IR http=off .
IPC,
.BR fail2zig\-client (1),
jails, bans, and state are unaffected. Default:
.IR true .
.TP
.B metrics_bind
String (IP address). Address the HTTP metrics server binds to. Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
Do not expose publicly without additional access controls.
.TP
.B metrics_port
Integer (1\(en65535). Port for the HTTP server. Default:
.IR 9100 .
The server exposes
.IR /metrics ,
.IR /api/status ,
and
.IR /events
(WebSocket). 0 is rejected; it does not disable the endpoint. Use
.BR "metrics_enabled = false" .
.TP
.B firewall
String. Which firewall backend to use.
.I auto
probes nftables, then ipset, then iptables and uses the first that is usable.
.IR nftables ,
.IR ipset ,
or
.I iptables
probes only that backend; if it is unusable,
.B on_no_backend
decides. There is no fallback to another backend. Unknown values are
rejected with line and column context. Default:
.IR auto .
.TP
.B on_no_backend
String. What happens when an enforcing jail exists but no usable backend was
found.
.I fail-closed
exits with the cause logged.
.I log-only
keeps running DEGRADED: bans are logged, not applied, and
.BR fail2zig\-client (1)
.B status
shows
.IR "Protection: DEGRADED (cause)" .
Default:
.IR fail-closed .
.
.SH DEFAULTS SECTION
All keys in this section apply to every jail unless overridden in the
.BI [jails. name ]
section.
.TP
.B bantime
Integer (seconds). Ban duration for a first offense. Minimum: 1. Default: 600.
.TP
.B findtime
Integer (seconds). Sliding window for counting failures. Minimum: 1. Default: 600.
.TP
.B maxretry
Integer. Number of failures within
.B findtime
required to trigger a ban. Minimum: 1. Default: 5.
.TP
.B banaction
String. Whether the jail enforces or observes.
.BR nftables ,
.BR iptables ,
and
.B ipset
all mean enforce with the backend selected by
.BR global.firewall ;
the names are accepted for fail2ban compatibility and do not select a
backend.
.B log-only
observes and never touches the firewall. Default:
.IR nftables .
.TP
.B ignoreip
String array. CIDR ranges and exact IPs that are never banned. Example:
.IR ["127.0.0.1/8", "::1", "10.0.0.0/8"] .
Default: empty.
.TP
.B source
String: auto, file, journald, or internal. Default: auto. Inherited by jails.
Auto uses existing log files, then supported journald input; recidive can use
internal confirmed-ban events. Explicit journald supports sshd; internal
supports recidive. Journald and internal sources require no logpath.
.TP
.B backend
Deprecated source alias for fail2ban compatibility (systemd means journald).
Do not specify both source and backend in the same section. It does not select
a firewall backend; use global.firewall.
.TP
.B bantime_increment_enabled
Boolean. Enable escalating ban durations for repeat offenders. Default:
.IR false .
.TP
.B bantime_increment_multiplier
Positive integer or decimal. Base multiplier in the escalation formula. Default: 1.
.TP
.B bantime_increment_factor
Nonnegative integer or decimal. Growth rate in the escalation formula. Default: 1.
.TP
.B bantime_increment_formula
String.
.B linear
or
.BR exponential .
.I linear:
.IR "bantime × multiplier × (1 + factor × n)" .
.I exponential:
.IR "bantime × multiplier × factor^n" .
Default:
.IR linear .
.TP
.B bantime_increment_max_bantime
Integer (seconds). Cap on escalated ban durations. Default: 604800 (7 days).
.
.SH JAIL SECTIONS
Each
.BI [jails. name ]
section defines one jail. The name must be ASCII alphanumeric, hyphens, or
underscores.
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. When false, the jail is parsed but not started. Default:
.IR true .
.TP
.B filter
String. Built-in filter name or a name resolvable via the filter registry.
Accepts hyphenated and underscore forms interchangeably. An enabled jail must
name a supported built-in filter; empty or unknown names fail validation.
.TP
.B logpath
String array. Absolute paths to log files. Missing files are warned about but
are not fatal — they may appear after the daemon starts.
.TP
.B source
Overrides defaults.source. Journald and internal jails do not need logpath.
.TP
.B maxretry
Optional integer (1–128). Overrides
.B defaults.maxretry
for this jail.
.TP
.B findtime
Optional integer (seconds). Overrides
.B defaults.findtime
for this jail.
.TP
.B bantime
Optional integer (seconds). Overrides
.B defaults.bantime
for this jail.
.TP
.B banaction
Optional string. Overrides
.B defaults.banaction
for this jail.
.TP
.B ignoreip
Optional string array. Replaces (does not merge with)
.B defaults.ignoreip
for this jail.
.TP
.B bantime_increment_enabled , bantime_increment_multiplier , bantime_increment_factor , bantime_increment_formula , bantime_increment_max_bantime
Per-jail values take precedence over
.B [defaults]
values; jails without an explicit setting inherit from defaults.
.B bantime_increment_multiplier
and
.B bantime_increment_factor
accept either integer or fractional values (e.g.
.B factor = 1.5
for a softer escalation curve).
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Minimal configuration
.nf
[global]
memory_ceiling_mb = 64

[defaults]
bantime   = 600
findtime  = 600
maxretry  = 5
banaction = "nftables"
ignoreip  = ["127.0.0.1/8", "::1"]

[jails.sshd]
enabled = true
filter  = "sshd"
logpath = ["/var/log/auth.log"]
.fi
.PP
.SS SSH with exponential escalation
.nf
[defaults]
bantime                       = 600
findtime                      = 600
maxretry                      = 5
banaction                     = "nftables"
ignoreip                      = ["127.0.0.1/8", "::1"]
bantime_increment_enabled     = true
bantime_increment_formula     = "exponential"
bantime_increment_multiplier  = 1
bantime_increment_factor      = 2
bantime_increment_max_bantime = 1209600

[jails.sshd]
enabled  = true
filter   = "sshd"
logpath  = ["/var/log/auth.log", "/var/log/secure"]
maxretry = 3
bantime  = 3600
.fi
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fail2zig (1),
.BR fail2zig\-client (1)
.PP
Full reference:
.UR https://fail2zig.com/docs/reference/config/
.UE
.
.SH HISTORY
The fail2zig.toml format was introduced in fail2zig 0.1.0.
.B firewall
and
.B metrics_enabled
were added in fail2zig 0.3.1.
